    "title": "EFV neuropsychiatric toxicity: insomnia and vivid dreams",
    "message": "Guidelines note EFV frequently causes neuropsychiatric effects including insomnia, vivid dreams and dizziness, typically within the first 2-6 weeks of therapy. This patient started EFV in February 2024 and now reports several weeks of poor sleep and vivid dreams, which are classic EFV toxicity symptoms listed in the adverse event monitoring checklist. Evidence for drug attribution: symptoms match the guideline-described EFV toxicity profile exactly. Evidence against: onset is late relative to the typical 2-6 week window, and non-drug causes such as depression, anxiety or substance use have not been excluded. The clinician's plan documents the complaint but proposes no management or regimen change.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Screen for depression, anxiety and substance use using validated tools; consider EFV substitution per guideline toxicity management if symptoms persist or worsen.",
