    "title": "Neuropsychiatric adverse event not flagged for aDSM reporting",
    "message": "Guidelines require active screening for neuropsychiatric symptoms including bad dreams, insomnia, anxiety and mood changes at every visit for patients on EFV, with suspected adverse drug reactions documented and reported through adverse drug surveillance (aDSM) channels. This patient's insomnia and vivid dreams were recorded at intake but no adverse event documentation, reporting form, or follow-up monitoring plan appears in today's assessment. The encounter also lacks any mental health screening despite guideline emphasis on diagnosing depression and anxiety with brief validated instruments.",
